WEBVTT

00:02.102 --> 00:03.569
Legend has it...

00:04.738 --> 00:07.536
...that during the Heian Period, there
were men who fought with no weapons.

00:07.875 --> 00:13.211
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.681 --> 00:19.846
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:32.966 --> 00:40.395
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.674 --> 00:46.510
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.048 --> 00:53.953
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.622 --> 00:59.388
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.493 --> 01:02.690
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.466 --> 01:13.531
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:13.707 --> 01:19.543
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.414 --> 01:27.684
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:27.854 --> 01:36.262
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:36.964 --> 01:38.625
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.375 --> 01:51.811
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

01:53.146 --> 01:56.411
Of the Niten Ichi Style,
Lord Iori Miyamoto!

02:00.454 --> 02:03.821
Of the Mutsu Enmei Style,
Lady Tsubura Mutsu!

02:07.361 --> 02:10.762
Of the Yagyu Shinkage Style,
Lord Jubei Yagyu!

02:15.969 --> 02:17.960
Finally, Lord Takato!

02:25.379 --> 02:29.716
<i>The Successor</i>

02:29.716 --> 02:31.115
That is all.
<i>The Successor</i>

02:31.818 --> 02:35.754
Those of you who have won in the
presence of the Shogun shall move on...

02:35.889 --> 02:38.084
...to the elimination round
after a short rest.

02:38.792 --> 02:40.919
Please rest in your
respective waiting rooms.

02:41.028 --> 02:43.553
We will inform you of
the match-ups shortly.

02:46.933 --> 02:49.060
Please, rest in this room.

02:52.706 --> 02:55.004
Now then, Lord Takato, this way, please.

02:55.175 --> 02:56.437
I'll stay with them.

02:56.610 --> 02:57.406
But, that's...

03:03.183 --> 03:06.641
Now it all hinges on what kind of
match-ups Iemitsu comes up with.

03:06.787 --> 03:08.379
It's all about luck from here on in.

03:08.522 --> 03:09.386
Luck?

03:09.523 --> 03:13.015
The first lucky break we need
is you not facing Jubei.

03:13.894 --> 03:15.987
So you're saying that I
can't beat him, but you can?

03:16.129 --> 03:18.154
Yes, because I'm powerful...

03:18.832 --> 03:21.096
At least, that's what I want to say...

03:22.903 --> 03:25.303
But the odds aren't too good.

03:29.543 --> 03:31.340
The other big break we need...

03:31.445 --> 03:34.744
Is for me to defeat
Jubei in the tournament.

03:35.282 --> 03:38.683
Are you saying that even you
have no way of beating Jubei?

03:39.353 --> 03:41.150
I can't think of any right now!

03:46.093 --> 03:47.617
Please, pardon me.

03:50.931 --> 03:53.422
Here are the match-ups
for the tournament.

03:58.772 --> 03:59.932
Here it is!

04:07.247 --> 04:09.681
Well, that first big
break we were hoping for...

04:09.783 --> 04:11.307
It's not happening.

04:11.485 --> 04:16.354
Tsubura, your first opponent in
the elimination round is Jubei.

04:36.410 --> 04:39.709
Lady Mutsu, Lord Takato, it is time.

04:39.846 --> 04:40.972
Please prepare.

04:42.516 --> 04:44.040
Why don't you bail?

04:44.217 --> 04:46.481
Know what's waiting for you? A beast!

04:53.360 --> 04:54.793
Let's go, Sasuke.

04:54.895 --> 04:55.953
Right.

05:29.796 --> 05:33.664
If you keep scowling like
that, they'll be on to you.

05:38.071 --> 05:40.699
There's no way to take on everybody.

05:40.907 --> 05:43.637
For now, just focus on beating Jubei.

06:04.130 --> 06:09.363
We will now begin the first
match of the elimination round.

06:10.270 --> 06:15.833
To the east, of the Yagyu Shinkage
Style, Lord Hyogonosuke Yagyu.

06:16.710 --> 06:21.909
To the west, of the Niten Ichi
Style, Lord Iori Miyamoto.

06:26.686 --> 06:28.347
Tell me, Tajima...

06:29.089 --> 06:30.954
What will be the outcome of this match?

06:31.091 --> 06:34.424
My lord, I believe it
will be a close match.

06:34.594 --> 06:40.055
So even a master like yourself cannot
predict the outcome of this duel, eh?

06:42.202 --> 06:46.366
I still don't understand it.
Why isn't Iori using two swords?

06:46.740 --> 06:49.106
Is it really just a gimmick after all?

06:49.576 --> 06:52.704
Yes, it appears to be so, my lord.

06:52.812 --> 06:54.074
Your Highness?

06:54.915 --> 06:56.906
I do beg to differ.

06:57.417 --> 07:02.354
He merely did not need to draw
both swords to win that match.

07:02.656 --> 07:04.647
Hmm, is that so?

07:04.858 --> 07:08.658
Then I suppose we can look forward
to him drawing both this time!

07:10.730 --> 07:15.633
Let's see that two-sword
technique of yours this time, eh?

07:16.136 --> 07:22.006
Whether or not I use both shall depend
on your attack, Lord Hyogonosuke.

07:30.317 --> 07:32.285
What do you think will
happen in this match?

07:32.485 --> 07:35.648
I've heard people say
that the Owari Yagyu Clan...

07:35.755 --> 07:39.054
...is a cut above the Edo
Yagyu Clan in terms of skill...

07:39.159 --> 07:43.186
In all battles, there is something
called destiny in the cards.

07:43.330 --> 07:44.422
Destiny?

07:45.131 --> 07:49.261
If two swordsmen can battle each
other at the zenith of their powers...

07:49.402 --> 07:50.767
...then they're lucky.

07:51.705 --> 07:55.903
If I remember correctly, I believe that
Lord Hyogonosuke has some kind of...

07:56.009 --> 07:58.307
...history with Musashi Miyamoto.

07:58.445 --> 07:59.969
With Musashi Miyamoto?

08:00.113 --> 08:02.445
It happened about ten years ago...

08:02.749 --> 08:07.550
Lord Musashi and Lord Hyogonosuke
met for the first time in Owari.

08:07.687 --> 08:12.021
At the time, Lord Owari
was trying to hire Musashi.

08:12.158 --> 08:16.595
But Lord Hyogonosuke
dissuaded him with these words...

08:17.163 --> 08:20.496
"Musashi's sword can be
wielded by Musashi alone."

08:20.600 --> 08:24.297
"It is not by any means a technique
that can be passed on to others."

08:24.738 --> 08:28.970
I have heard that they did
not duel each other that day.

08:34.614 --> 08:35.603
Begin!

08:52.365 --> 08:56.062
That technique can't
be passed on... or can it?

08:56.703 --> 08:59.263
Now's a good time to
find out for yourself!

08:59.906 --> 09:04.206
To this day, I am confident
that my words were true.

09:04.678 --> 09:09.240
That ki from Musashi was the kind that
can only be generated by a genius!

09:15.088 --> 09:20.458
Should you be defeated, then
Musashi will have been defeated.

09:20.927 --> 09:23.259
As Lord Musashi himself
allegedly stated, correct?

09:24.097 --> 09:25.257
Indeed.

09:25.432 --> 09:28.765
But please don't assume incorrectly...

09:29.135 --> 09:32.502
I still have a long way to go
before I reach Lord Musashi's level.

09:32.906 --> 09:34.237
Is that so?

09:36.543 --> 09:39.376
Then I made a mistake, Musashi.

09:40.013 --> 09:43.449
For not facing you in combat
that day, when I had the chance.

09:44.150 --> 09:48.052
Now that I can feel my
skills slipping away with age...

09:48.922 --> 09:51.720
...there is nothing on
Earth that I regret more!

10:01.901 --> 10:03.027
Well!

10:05.038 --> 10:06.403
I see...

10:06.673 --> 10:10.040
This is the Go-no-sen move, made
possible by Musashi's unique...

10:10.176 --> 10:11.939
...Issun no Mikiri technique, eh?

10:14.714 --> 10:17.911
It looked to me as
though Iori was late, but...

10:18.618 --> 10:20.745
That was the
Go-no-sen, just now...

10:20.854 --> 10:26.486
By making him attack first, he's able
to anticipate his opponent's next move.

10:26.826 --> 10:31.627
The opponent won't realize this until it's
too late. It requires great skill!

10:33.800 --> 10:34.630
But...

10:41.107 --> 10:42.005
He's safe!

10:42.308 --> 10:42.831
Wait...

10:52.719 --> 10:55.415
His shadow was already
gone at the time of attack.

10:55.555 --> 10:57.614
They call that technique
the Moon Shadow.

11:13.740 --> 11:14.866
It's over, huh?

11:15.074 --> 11:15.972
Yes.

11:16.543 --> 11:18.534
Iori wins the match!

11:22.715 --> 11:24.239
Father!

11:26.753 --> 11:27.685
Two swords!

11:27.787 --> 11:29.254
When did that happen?

11:29.989 --> 11:30.921
Huh!

11:31.758 --> 11:34.659
At the same time that he was blocking
the Moon Shadow with his long sword...

11:34.761 --> 11:37.787
...he drew his wakizashi
and slashed his torso!

11:40.667 --> 11:42.362
S-Stop!

11:45.004 --> 11:46.699
Well, well! That was splendid!

11:46.806 --> 11:48.774
I had an excellent view
of the two-sword technique!

11:53.746 --> 11:54.838
Lord Tenkai...

12:01.321 --> 12:03.016
An Owari, perhaps...

12:03.122 --> 12:07.081
...but all the same, a fellow Shinkage
Style master has just been defeated...

12:07.293 --> 12:11.753
Your back is up against the wall
now, eh? Yagyu Shinkage Style!

12:12.565 --> 12:16.968
The next match-up is Jubei versus
Mutsu. What do you think, Tajima?

12:17.437 --> 12:20.895
I guarantee that it will go
as you wish, Your Highness.

12:21.574 --> 12:22.836
Jubei!

12:23.109 --> 12:26.169
So you're the only one I can call
on to defend the honor of the...

12:26.279 --> 12:28.873
...Yagyu Shinkage Style after all?

12:29.249 --> 12:31.877
We now move on to the second match
of the elimination tournament.

12:32.051 --> 12:36.613
To the east, of the Yagyu Shinkage
Style, Lord Jubei Yagyu.

12:36.923 --> 12:40.859
To the west, of the Mutsu Enmei
Style, Lady Tsubura Mutsu.

12:43.963 --> 12:45.794
Don't try too hard, now.

12:45.899 --> 12:47.924
It's not a matter of life
and death if you lose.

12:53.940 --> 12:55.601
I'm not going to lose.

13:01.180 --> 13:03.205
You've come to the end of the line.

13:03.516 --> 13:06.542
You won't be drawing
that Muramasa, Sasuke.

13:06.653 --> 13:09.213
Well, we'll just see about that, sir.

13:10.857 --> 13:11.687
You!

13:27.173 --> 13:31.507
I would have preferred to
meet a male Mutsu in battle...

13:32.345 --> 13:36.304
Jubei, is it really that
embarrassing to lose to a girl?

13:44.223 --> 13:45.315
Begin!

13:55.535 --> 13:56.593
Begin!

14:48.354 --> 14:49.787
Ah!

14:53.559 --> 14:55.117
Interesting!

15:03.970 --> 15:05.164
Surely not!

15:05.271 --> 15:06.932
Jubei couldn't possibly...

15:07.340 --> 15:11.674
I was wondering how good a
swordsman he was, it's as I'd hoped!

15:13.046 --> 15:16.413
So the Yagyu Shinkage
Style is history now, eh?

15:16.949 --> 15:18.007
It's not over yet.

15:22.789 --> 15:23.778
I can win!

15:24.090 --> 15:26.024
If that's the best he can do...

15:32.365 --> 15:34.390
Say your prayers, Jubei!

15:36.035 --> 15:37.002
What?

15:58.124 --> 15:59.421
I can't move!

16:00.827 --> 16:02.192
What's going on?

16:03.496 --> 16:05.157
He's going for the kill now!

16:10.470 --> 16:11.596
What the hell...

16:11.938 --> 16:13.098
What's this ki?

16:48.841 --> 16:49.933
What happened?

16:50.076 --> 16:52.738
I can't really tell from
here what's happening!

16:58.284 --> 16:59.615
Good job of dodging!

17:00.186 --> 17:02.552
Dammit, it's no good. I can't beat him!

17:06.459 --> 17:07.483
In that case...

17:08.694 --> 17:09.718
It's over.

17:15.535 --> 17:16.229
Hey!

17:23.709 --> 17:26.143
We're not through yet, are we?

17:31.350 --> 17:32.840
What? You're not dodging?

17:35.855 --> 17:40.986
Now then, I leave the Young Miss
in your care, Lord Mutsu!

17:41.527 --> 17:43.495
So you're going to do it after all?

17:52.672 --> 17:53.331
A gauntlet?

17:55.208 --> 17:56.402
Mouth needles?

17:56.509 --> 17:57.407
What the hell?

18:27.473 --> 18:29.441
Samon! You must kill her at once!

18:29.575 --> 18:30.667
Huh? But...

18:30.977 --> 18:32.911
That woman's not a Mutsu!

18:35.848 --> 18:36.678
Young Miss!

18:40.853 --> 18:41.842
Iemitsu!

18:41.954 --> 18:44.582
I, Tsubura, the daughter
of Saemonnosuke Sanada...

18:44.690 --> 18:46.555
...have come to claim your head!

18:57.003 --> 19:00.336
With such pitiful skills, you call yourself
the nations' greatest swordsman?

19:00.706 --> 19:02.435
Samon! Jubei!

19:02.575 --> 19:04.167
We must protect the Shogun!

19:16.355 --> 19:20.655
Damn it! That blow I just
took from Jubei's bokuto...

19:20.860 --> 19:22.657
Die!

19:31.103 --> 19:34.129
Yagyu and Ono... No time to
stop those two from here...

19:39.712 --> 19:40.542
Sasuke!

19:42.181 --> 19:43.148
Young Miss!

19:43.949 --> 19:45.883
It's all right...

19:48.020 --> 19:53.219
This is what I've
always wanted, after all.

19:54.527 --> 19:56.290
Please escape, Young Miss!

19:58.264 --> 20:03.497
Lord Yukimura... it has taken me 20
years to catch up, but I, Sasuke...

20:12.712 --> 20:14.407
Now I die in battle too.

20:15.715 --> 20:16.977
Sasuke...

20:19.218 --> 20:21.209
Lord Takato...

20:22.421 --> 20:24.855
I have left the Young Miss to you.

20:25.024 --> 20:27.356
What better man than...

20:32.098 --> 20:34.566
Sasuke! Please don't die!

20:38.104 --> 20:38.798
Kill her!

20:38.904 --> 20:41.805
Tadatsune, Samon,
kill this woman now!

20:53.853 --> 20:56.014
Matajuuro! My sword!

20:56.255 --> 20:57.244
Here!

21:15.975 --> 21:20.844
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.991 --> 21:44.028
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:44.303 --> 21:54.042
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:54.180 --> 22:03.179
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:03.322 --> 22:13.994
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:15.034 --> 22:21.166
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:21.540 --> 22:24.532
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:25.344 --> 22:31.681
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.984 --> 22:37.479
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:52.304 --> 22:54.295
The Shogun's Tournament
has descended into chaos.

22:54.440 --> 22:56.806
Taking Iemitsu hostage, Takato
tries to escape with Tsubura.

22:56.909 --> 22:58.706
But Jubei stands in their way.

22:58.878 --> 23:00.209
Will Takato fight him?

23:00.746 --> 23:02.373
Next episode of the Age of Chaos...

23:02.648 --> 23:03.910
<i>The Beast</i>

23:04.016 --> 23:06.246
Pay close attention, and wait!
